[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_1
diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: FRRouting (bgpd within the frr.service) on leaf_router_0_1.
- Mechanism: With bgpd down on leaf_router_0_1, the 10.0.1.0/24 prefix is not advertised to the spines. Consequently, neither spine learns 10.0.1.0/24 and cannot re-advertise it to leaf_router_0_0. Leaf_router_0_0 therefore lacks a route to 10.0.1.0/24 and returns ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable” to pc_0_0, and the reverse path fails similarly from pc_0_1.
- Localization: On the edge leaf attached to pc_0_1 (leaf_router_0_1). Evidence:
  • frr on leaf_router_0_1 is failed: “frr.service … Active: failed (failed)”.
  • “show ip bgp summary” on leaf_router_0_1: “bgpd is not running”.
  • Spines show their neighbor to leaf_router_0_1 stuck in Active (down): spine_router_0_0 neighbor 172.16.0.7 and spine_router_0_1 neighbor 172.16.0.11 both Active.
  • Routing tables: leaf_router_0_0 has only connected routes (no 10.0.1.0/24), and both spines/super-spine carry only 10.0.0.0/24 via leaf_router_0_0; 10.0.1.0/24 is absent.
  • Host pings return net unreachable from their local leaf (10.0.0.1 / 10.0.1.1).
- Root cause: The FRR service (bgpd) is down on leaf_router_0_1, withdrawing 10.0.1.0/24 from the fabric.
- Corrective fix: Restart FRR on leaf_router_0_1 (systemctl restart frr) and confirm bgpd establishes with both spines and that 10.0.1.0/24 appears in spine and leaf_router_0_0 BGP/RIB tables. Ensure the service is enabled and investigate logs (/var/log/frr/) for the cause of the failure to prevent recurrence.

=== END ===